        <p>DR. J. COLLIS BROWNE S OHLOIiODYNE.</p>
        <p>THE ORIGINACiiii ONLY -GENUINE. CfiLORODYNE is admitted by the Profession to be the most wonderful and valuable remedy ever dis Isovered.</p>
        <p>CHLORODYNE is tbe best remedy known for Coughs, Consumption, Bronchitis and Asthma. CRLORODYNE effectually checks and arrests those too often fatal diseases—Diphtheria, Fever Croup Ague CIILORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhcea and is the only specific in Cholera and Dysentery. CILORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy. Hysteria, Pa!pitation, and Spasms. fiIiLORODyNE is the only palliative in Neural- gia, Rheumatism, Gout, Cancer, Toothache, Meningitis,</p>
        <p>From Dr. B. J. BOULTON AND Co., Horneastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne inour Practice lately and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ, and from whatevercause. It induces a feeling cf comfort and quietude not obtainable by any other remedy, and it seems to possess this great advantage over all ether sedatives ; that it lea .-es no unpleasant after effects. " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatca from her Majesty's Consul at Manilla to the effect that Cholera had been raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CHLORO- DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December. 1864. CAUTION.-BEwARE OF pi E ACY AND IMITA- T lONS. cAuTioN.—Vice-ChAneelior Sir W. PAGE WOOD stated that Dr. J. COLLIS BROWNE was, anioubtedly, the inventor of " CHLORODYNE and tba t the story of the defendant was ileliberatel uatrue. which he regretted to FREEMAN, say had been sworn to.—See Times, 13th July, 1864. Sold in bottles at Is. and 4s. 6d. None is genuine without the words " DR. j cows BRowNws CHLORODYNE "on the Government Stamp. Overwhelm- aoCompanies each bottle. ing MediOa testimony</p>
      </div>
