        <p>In connection with the above competition Wel effer a monthly prize of 5s to the competitor who i succeeds n placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winners' score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next months competition. The winner may re- enter the tourney if he chooses, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as follows: Two for the correct solution of a prob- lem ; two for correcting the author's terms, one for showing a dual solution or a dual key-move. and one for showing's dual continuation at any stage in the solution. As will be noticed by the above list, several of our solvers found a dual key move to Problem No. 66, by 18-15, 10-19, 26-23, &amp;c. We have accord- ingly awarded those solvers the extra point each.</p>
