      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-01-19_WidnesExaminer_art0084" n="art0084">
        <head>Runcorn Petty Sessions.</head>
        <p>Runcorn Petty Sessions.</p>
        <p>Beore Mes ere. A. ThornAs (nresiOing) and Francis Wiswall.</p>
        <p>LICMING. DRUNICENN—E-9-3::i4DITCATION.— John Leach was granted authorlty to sell intoxicAnts at the Fox Tavern. Vic Ir-street, until next trans'er day.—Thomas Carrington. Duke-street, was fined be and 8s 6d costs for drunkenness.— William Evans, and John Ni..holls, both of Gilbert-street, were fined Is and 9s costs f•sr neglccting to send their several chi'dren to school.—Henry Bu-ton, a boatman, had to pay costs 4s 6d for keeping a dog without a license.</p>
