        <p>registered.—The- second half was jest as .devoid of interest as the first with one exception, and that was that Newton scored the only goal of the Match, Kenny doing the trick with a splendid obliTae shOr, Goal long range. LANCASHIRE ALLIANCE. Warrington v. Southport High Park. This match taok place on he greund of the termer, at sigh Ptrk, on Saturday. Pie.noint started operations on bohal of the visitors. Warringtln wont away in grand style. and Connor forced a corner, which, how- ever, proved abortive. Ead to end play ensued, both sets of backs clearing finely. From a gold clearance by Mather, Murray gained possession, and tricking the home back gave to Connor, who centred grandly to Pier. paint, whose iltlOt WAS itlit a trifle wide. This brought about half-time, with ueithe, sii having scored. South- port restarted the game. Following A good movement by Bryan, the visiting forwards indaiged in a fine series of passes, Pierpaiet eventually finding the net with a grand'shot. Connor ran well down the wing and centred to Pierpoint, who notched the second goal with a beauti- ful MIA. The scores at the olricithba of the game stood: Warrington, two goals ; Southpirt High Park, nil.</p>
