        <p>MARRIAGE. JOHNSON—CooK—January 7th, at the Parish Church, War- rington, by the Rev. A. F. White, James Johnson to Esther Cook. DEATHS. Caosar—January 7th, at 15, Kendrick-street, Warrington, Emily Augusta Crosby, aged 42 years. Tatomasorr—Jauuary 2nd, at Thewlis-street, Warrington, Alexander Thomason, aged 44 years. BaowN—January sth, at Parr-street, Warrington, Mary Brown, aged 75 years. HousToN—January sth, at Bewsey-road, Warrington, Martha , Houston, aged b 5 years. SYKEV—January 7th, at Orford-lane, Warrington, Mary Sykes, aged 80 years. LEATHER—January Bth, Lord Nelsoa-street, Warrington, Ann Leather, aged 70 years. 1117GHES—January 10th, at Kent-street, Warrington, James Hughes, aged 48 years. ASHURST—January 15th, at 47, Bridge-street, Warrington. Jane, widow of the late Charles Ashurst, formerly Station Master of Bank Quay, Warrington, aged 62. Friends kindly ac:ept this, the only intimation, IN MEMORIAM. In loving memory of my dear Mother Hannah Owen, who fell asleep Jaauary 17th, 1897. aged 70 years.—Gene but not forgotten:</p>
